test.yaml:13:16: this step checks out code from a pull request (github.event.pull_request.head.ref) in a "pull_request_target" workflow and "make" runs it afterwards. an environment lets the job start, but github.event.pull_request.head.ref is not a commit: whoever wrote the pull request can push to it after the check (an approval, a label, a comment) and the job runs what is there then, not what was reviewed. the workflow has a write token and secrets, so whoever controls that code can use them. check out the commit that was reviewed ("github.event.pull_request.head.sha") and not the branch [untrusted-checkout]
test.yaml:22:16: this step checks out code from a pull request (github.event.pull_request.head.sha) in a "pull_request_target" workflow and "make" runs it afterwards. a label condition lets the job start, but it stays true after the review: the workflow runs again for each push to the pull request, so the code of a new push runs with the label although nobody has looked at it. the workflow has a write token and secrets, so whoever controls that code can use them. run only for the "labeled" event and check out the commit of that event, or take the label away in the job ("gh pr edit --remove-label") [untrusted-checkout]
